--- a/docs/eval_harness_design.md
+++ b/docs/eval_harness_design.md
@@ -18,6 +18,15 @@
 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## CI Gating with Thresholds
+- `frai eval` accepts `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (can be used multiple times) to gate CI jobs on metric scores.
+- Thresholds must be metric IDs known to the evaluator and min values between 0 and 1.
+- Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass; exit code 1 if any threshold fails; exit code 2 if threshold usage is invalid (malformed, unknown metric, out-of-range value).
+- Reports gain top-level `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold.
+- Metrics with null scores (e.g., exact_match without references) fail their thresholds instead of crashing.
+- SDK users access this via `generateReport` with optional `thresholds` object argument.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
